    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is led today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (78.08), our two most formidable starts. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor and a solid matchup against a mid-tier arm, while **Kyle Tucker** showcases his elite floor despite a potentially tougher environment. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Andy Pages** (73.98) also provide high-efficiency production, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically highlighted for his stolen base upside against a pitcher susceptible to a slow delivery. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.11) round out the high-upside core, utilizing strong lineup placement and favorable wind conditions to boost their output above baseline projections. \n\nTactically, we are banking on the dynamic platoon advantages provided to **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (+14%) and **Curtis Mead** (+10%) as they look to exploit their matchup. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Josh Jung**, whose 53.35 score fell just short of the active roster threshold. While **Josh Jung** offered solid park factors, the superior efficiency and platoon-alignment of the middle-infield options forced him to the bench. We are tracking a few risks: **Dominic Smith** and **Andy Pages** are subject to \"Lineup Pending\" fluctuations, and while the wind is blowing out to assist our power hitters, any late-scratch adjustments for these players will require immediate roster recalibration to protect our daily game caps.",
